We are honored to welcome Julio Della Flora, one of Brazil’s leading experts when it comes to exploiting and protecting devices at the hardware layer.

Julio is an Embedded Security Researcher and Red Team Leader at P1 Infosec, as well as the person behind the popular YouTube channel “Hardware Hacking.”

With more than 10 years of experience in information security, he has spoken at major industry events such as H2HC, YSTS, and MindTheSec. He is also the author of globally recognized vulnerabilities (CVE-2018-20823 and CVE-2019-12762).

In his talk, “Tools for Hardware Hacking,” he will share the essential devices and tools for hardware exploitation practices.
